title: The Right calls a vote of no confidence against the current government!
subtitle: We have angered our coalition partners too much...
new-page: true
on-arrival: tried_supporting_collectivist = 0; unionist_relation -= 5 if not in_social_catholic_coalition; gold_relation -= 5 if in_grand_coalition; ddp_relation -= 5 if not in_social_catholic_coalition; lvp_relation -= 5 if in_weimar_coalition and not in_social_catholic_coalition or in_grand_coalition; lvp_right += 2 if in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition; gold_right += 2 if in_grand_coalition; ddp_right += 1; dufour_angry += 20
on-departure: secularized = 0
view-if: chancellor_party == "Marcher" and marcher_in_government = 1 and ((in_grand_coalition = 1 or in_popular_front = 1 or in_minority_government = 1 or (in_social_catholic_coalition and concord_formed) and coalition_dissent >= 3)) or (in_weimar_coalition = 1 and not (in_social_catholic_coalition and concord_formed) and coalition_dissent >= 4) and marcher_r < 50 and not constructive_vonc
tags: event
go-to: vonc_menu

= Vote of No Confidence

[? if in_grand_coalition and not lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> ?][? if (in_grand_coalition or in_social_liberal_coalition) and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> ?][? if in_weimar_coalition or in_popular_front or in_minority_government and not in_social_liberal_coalition: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?][? if lvp_formed and not in_social_catholic_coalition:&nbsp;and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]?][? if in_social_liberal_coalition and not lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> ?] has called for a vote of no confidence against us, due to our various policies and disagreements. If this succeeds, there will likely be an election in a few months.

@vonc_menu

- @try_assuage: Try to assuage our partners.
- @support_kpd: Could we get the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> to abstain?
- @support_kpd_left: Could we form a United Left coalition with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>?
- @let_it_happen: Let the vote happen.

@try_assuage

How do we assuage our partners?

- @dvp_prussia_2: Let the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> into Heartland.
- @give_up_prussia: Give up on leadership of Heartland.
- @austerity: Enact a massive austerity plan.
- @resources: Use our resources to reduce dissent within the coalition.
- @support_kpd: Could we get the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> to abstain?
- @support_kpd_left: Could we form a United Left coalition with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>?
- @let_it_happen: Never mind. Let the vote happen.

@dvp_prussia_2
view-if: year <= 1929 and in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0 and (in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland) and in_grand_coalition = 1 and gold_was_in_heartland == 0 and not lvp_formed
choose-if: unionist_leader != "Renck" and not secularized
unavailable-subtitle: [? if unionist_leader = "Renck": Renck and the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] strongly dissents against. ?]
on-arrival: in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 1; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; gold_relation += 10; unionist_relation -= 5; ddp_relation += 3; coalition_dissent -= 1; left_dissent += 5; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 1; gold_left += 3; burgher_gold += 3

Letting the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> into the Heartland government is an offer too good for them to refuse, no matter their leadership. 

However, this has negatively impacted our freedom of action we previously had in the Unity coalition.

@give_up_prussia
subtitle: Bristol would need to resign.
view-if: heartland_leader = "Bristol" and neo_weimar_coalition_heartland >= 50
on-arrival: coalition_dissent = 1; heartland_leader = "Sedgewick"; heartland_leader = "Askew" if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick"; reformist_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 5; commons_marcher -= 5; burgher_marcher -= 5; landed_marcher -= 3; braun_resign = 1

Fine. We no longer control the government of Heartland. The vote has been called off.

The Minister-President position is transferred to the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].

@austerity
view-if: welfare >= 0 and not secularized
on-arrival: coalition_dissent = 0; commons_marcher -= 10; disfavored_marcher -= 10; commons_collectivist += 7; commons_royalist += 3; disfavored_collectivist += 5; disfavored_royalist += 5; left_dissent += 15; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 15; reformist_dissent += 5; welfare -= 2; budget += 1; disfavored += 3; collectivist_coalition_dissent += 1; collectivist_relation -= 10 if in_popular_front; goal_marcher_cancel += 1; social_welfare_timer = 10

Fine. We enacted a massive austerity program to cut welfare, in order to maintain the stability of our coalition. The vote has been called off.

@resources
view-if: secularized = 0
choose-if: (resources >= 3 and in_weimar_coalition or in_popular_front or in_minority_government) or ((resources >= 3 and in_grand_coalition and not (gold_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and not lvp_formed) or (resources >= 3 and (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition) and not (lvp_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and lvp_formed))
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 3: We do not have enough resources. ?] [? if in_grand_coalition and (gold_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and not lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> doesn't want our resources anymore. ?] [? if (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition) and (lvp_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> doesn't want our resources anymore. ?]
subtitle: -3 resources
on-arrival: resources -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1;

By transferring resources to our coalition partners, we can reduce their dissent against our policies. This is a crude, but effective solution.

@support_kpd
choose-if: ((in_grand_coalition and communist_coalition >= 3 and collectivist_relation >= 50 and collectivist_r >= gold_r and not lvp_formed) or (in_grand_coalition and communist_coalition >= 3 and collectivist_relation >= 50 and collectivist_r >= (lvp_r / 2) and lvp_formed)) or (in_weimar_coalition and collectivist_relation >= 50 and collectivist_r >= unionist_r and communist_coalition >= 3)
view-if: tried_supporting_collectivist = 0 and not in_popular_front
on-arrival: tried_supporting_collectivist = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if communist_coalition < 3 : The <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> won't take part in parliamentary government. ?] [? if collectivist_relation < 50 : The <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> is not friendly enough with us. ?] [? if ((in_grand_coalition and collectivist_r < gold_r and not lvp_formed) or (in_grand_coalition and collectivist_r < (lvp_r / 2) and lvp_formed)) or (in_weimar_coalition and collectivist_r < unionist_r): The <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> does not have enough votes. ?] [? if in_popular_front : We are already in a Popular Front with the <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span>. ?]

If the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> abstain, then we essentially can maintain a minority government[? if president=="DuFour":, although it would be very difficult to make policy without the support of President DuFour, which we do not have ?]. If this happens, then we will own a massive debt to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>. This could lead to broader cooperation in the future, for better or for worse.

- @support_kpd_2: Persuade the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> to "tolerate" us?
- @let_it_happen: Never mind. Let the vote happen.

@support_kpd_2
on-arrival: communist_coalition += 1; commons_collectivist += 3; collectivist_relation += 5
go-to: support_kpd_weimar if in_weimar_coalition; support_kpd_grand if in_grand_coalition


The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is not interested in a "toleration" arrangement; they will only support us if they can participate in the government as part of a coalition. And, if this toleration agreement happens, the right-wing parties will not be inclined to support us. 

@support_kpd_grand
on-arrival: support_collectivist_grand = 1

- @election_1928.popular_front_coalition: Form a "Popular Front" coalition?
- @election_1928.left_coalition
- @try_assuage: Never mind. We must deal with this some other way.

@support_kpd_weimar
on-arrival: support_collectivist_weimar = 1

- @election_1928.left_coalition
- @try_assuage: Never mind. We must deal with this some other way.

@support_kpd_left
subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> [? if sapd_formed: + <span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span> ?] ([+ left_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">Marchers</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> [? if sapd_formed: + <span style="color: #9B0000;">Laborists</span> ?] ([+ left_coalition +]%). [? if collectivist_relation < 50 : We do not have adequate relations with the <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span>. ?][? if communist_coalition < 3 : The <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> are too committed to their radical ways to partake in government. ?] [? if rubicon: - Why the hell would DuFour allow this? ?] [? if president_ideology != "Left" and president != "DuFour": - President [+ president +] is fiercely opposed to <span style="color: #9B0000;">Reformist</span> governance. ?]
view-if: in_popular_front
choose-if: left_coalition >= 50 and (collectivist_relation >= 50 or (collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" and collectivist_relation >= 40)) and communist_coalition >= 3 and not rubicon and president_ideology == "Left" or president == "DuFour"
go-to: election_1928.left_coalition_success

@let_it_happen
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_popular_front = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Unionist"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "Gold"; finance_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist"; labor_minister = "Sedgewick"; interior_minister = "Werth"; finance_minister = "Moldren"; economic_minister = "Curthose"; justice_minister = "Penn"; foreign_minister = "Stratton" if not stresemann_dead; foreign_minister = "Curthose" if stresemann_dead; agriculture_minister = "Dietrich"; army_minister = "Ravabelle"; coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 4; guild_marcher -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 2; commons_marcher -= 3 if pro_republic < 50; commons_marcher -= 4 if pro_republic < 40; guild_royalist += 4 if pro_republic < 50; burgher_royalist += 3 if pro_republic < 50
go-to: let_it_happen_hindenburg if president_ideology != "Left"; let_it_happen_braun if president_ideology == "Left"

@let_it_happen_hindenburg
on-arrival: chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; welfare -= 2; bruning_event_timer = 6 if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930
go-to: elections if bruning_event_seen or year < 1930

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Chancellor Askew has been appointed as the head of a new cabinet, consisting solely of the propertied parties. He immediately proceeds to cut welfare spending substantially.

[? if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930: New elections haven't been called yet but it's likely that they will be soon, considering Askew most likely doesn't have the majority of the Assembly behind him. ?]

@elections
call: set_next_election_time

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].

@let_it_happen_braun
on-arrival: marcher_caretaker = 1
call: set_next_election_time

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] remains as the head of a caretaker government, but no longer has the power to enact new policies.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].
